  <notes>FR-D11. COMPLETED 2026-08-06.
  Mechanism (approach b, deterministic push — see reasoning): the reactive proactive-suggest turn
  (022) is a probabilistic LLM selection over ≤3 chips and would not reliably satisfy "the chip
  appears for a loaded document"; instead the Reanalyze Binding id is resolved via the SAME
  capability-discovery seam every other bindingId in ConversationPane uses (consumerType
  `chat-summarize` + consumerCode `reanalyze`, disambiguated from the pre-existing Chat Summarize
  Binding), then deterministically pushed onto the reactive `useConsumerChips` surface: (1)
  immediately on a document-context tab focus if the bindingId is already resolved; (2) a catch-up
  effect once the bindingId resolves later; (3) persisted across every subsequent chip carrier via
  `getAppendedLocalChips`. Click routes through the existing `chips.acceptChips`/`dispatchBinding`
  → `dispatchConsumer` Click path — no new endpoint, no new decider (ADR-039 clean).
  `useConsumerChips.tsx` was edited additively: `acceptChips` now de-dupes `getAppendedLocalChips`
  output against `parsed` by bindingId (prevents double-render when a caller seeds the same chip
  both directly and via the append seam) — zero behavior change for any pre-existing caller.
  Step 9.5 review caught and fixed a real bug pre-merge: the catch-up effect originally depended on
  the whole (unstable) `chips` object and neither seed path guarded against an in-flight dispatch,
  which could have re-populated the strip mid-dispatch. Fixed with stable deps + dispatching/hasChips
  ref guards; locked in by a new regression test.
  Tests: ConversationPane.reanalyze-chip.e2e.test.tsx (5 tests — appears deterministically even
  with empty proactive-suggest result; absent for non-document context; click dispatches via
  dispatchConsumer; dark mode; no mid-dispatch re-seed). Full conversation suite: 626/626 green.
  typecheck: Surface-owned 0. Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check: PASS (no violations; ADR-039/021/028
  compliant). No new endpoint/decider added.</notes>
